          "answer": "11",
          "solution": "For each of the parallelograms $A B C O, C D E O$, EFAO in the diagram, half of its area is from the shaded triangle. Hence the triangle is half of the hexagon formed by the three parallelograms. Since the hexagon is made of 22 triangles, the shaded triangle must have area $11 \\mathrm{~cm}^{2}$.  ![](https://cdn.mathpix.com/cropped/2023_12_27_0f4ed2787981bb911326g-116.jpg?height=402&width=437&top_left_y=336&top_left_x=1392)",
